WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.480
It's time to meet another do-gooder or Drew-Gooder.

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.540
as we like to call them around here.

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.720
According to the National Restaurant Association,

4
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.650
over 100,000 restaurants have closed across the country

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.890
since the beginning of the pandemic.

6
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.190
An award-winning food blogger from Phoenix, Arizona

7
00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:22.290
has made it her mission to help restaurants

8
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:26.560
in her area to avoid a part of, excuse me,

9
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.920
to avoid being part of that statistic.

10
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.920
Diana Brandt, AKA AZ Foodie, made headlines

11
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.240
after she launched a fundraiser to help give back

12
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.380
to struggling restaurants and food vendors.

13
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.180
And she's been using the funds

14
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.390
she raised to leave tips at these restaurants,

15
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:48.000
sometimes as much as a thousand dollars.

16
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.823
So please welcome Diana to the show.

17
00:00:50.823 --> 00:00:53.573
(audience claps)

18
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.560
I love the way that you are handling wanting to give back.

19
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:04.840
I find it so unique, so impressionable, so actionable.

20
00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.460
You're just dropping giant tips.

21
00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.050
Yeah, so I have this platform

22
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.670
called AZ Foodie on Instagram.

23
00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:19.618 line:15%
And what I started doing, especially when COVID hit,

24
00:01:19.618 --> 00:01:23.810 line:15%
was just the connections that I've built in the community

25
00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.710 line:15%
and the family and the support,

26
00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:31.710 line:15%
I saw how they were suffering and how they were struggling.

27
00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.670
So many of my friends were scared to lose these businesses

28
00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:39.420
that they had built up over the last seven years.

29
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.610
And I felt like I needed to do something.

30
00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:44.830
And so initially when COVID hits,

31
00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:49.340
I started selling T-shirts, and then we also did a raffle.

32
00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:54.340
And we ended up raising $46,000 for 32 local restaurants.

33
00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.550
And that money was used to help keep their employees,

34
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.460
keep the lights on, all that kind of stuff.

35
00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:06.270 line:15%
And so each week, we're able to go out

36
00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:10.631
and give these tips that are $1,000,

37
00:02:10.631 --> 00:02:14.580 line:15%
and really just shock and surprise them.

38
00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.880 line:15%
Actually, I believe the money

39
00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.480 line:15%
goes to the entire restaurant, is that correct?

40
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.850 line:15%
Yes, it goes to the entire restaurant.

41
00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.230 line:15%
If they have a couple of employees there,

42
00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:28.220
that might happen as well.

43
00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:33.100
The other day we gave to a restaurant called Verdura.

44
00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.220
And the owner was there and we gave it to her,

45
00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.240
and she was just in so much shock and just so happy

46
00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.257
because those tips were gonna go to her employees

47
00:02:44.257 --> 00:02:47.670
who aren't making the same amount of tips.

48
00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.940 line:15%
And so they're struggling to pay their bills.

49
00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.010 line:15%
So she was like, hey, this, this money is gonna

50
00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:55.120 line:15%
help my employee pay their rent this month.

51
00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.780
And being so close to it,

52
00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.600
it's a very emotional experience to do.

53
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:06.600
Diana, wow, really, I have so much admiration

54
00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:11.360
and respect for everything you're doing.

55
00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:16.067
When we had heard about what you had done at the restaurant

56
00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:18.330
you just mentioned Verdura,

57
00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.340
it's funny because I invited Julia here.

58
00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.830
I can't believe you were talking about it.

59
00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:27.357
I was like, (mutters) Julia, hi.

60
00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:32.100
(audience claps)

61
00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.217
Hi, how's it going?

62
00:03:33.217 --> 00:03:35.134
Hi Diana, hi everybody.

63
00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.800
Thank you so much for having us.

64
00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.100
We appreciate you so immensely.

65
00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.900
And everything that you're doing resonated with us so much.

66
00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.700
And you know, we appreciate it

67
00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:46.870
from the bottom of our hearts.

68
00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.020
Thank you, Diana.

69
00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:49.113
And thank you, Drew.

70
00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:53.203
See, surprise Diana, by the way,

71
00:03:53.203 --> 00:03:57.817
nobody mess with Julia, or you're gonna get it.

72
00:03:57.817 --> 00:03:58.993
(audience laughs)

73
00:03:58.993 --> 00:04:02.410
Hello gentlemen, thank you for being with us today.

74
00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:07.170
And Verdura is Spanish for vegetable.

75
00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.460
And you are a vegan restaurant, correct?

76
00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:14.460
Yeah, so we're 100% vegan, located in uptown Phoenix.

77
00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:17.040
We've been through the ringer, in terms of COVID,

78
00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.450
closed three times now.

79
00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.580
And thank you to Diana's generosity

80
00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.140
for really showing our staff how important

81
00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.090
it means for us to stay in business,

82
00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:28.410
and most importantly, show them our appreciation.

83
00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:33.410
Well, you know, our friends at the plant-based company

84
00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:38.190
Field Roast wanted to join in on the tipping too,

85
00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:42.500
because Diana has inspired all of us, including them.

86
00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.850
And we would love to leave a $5,000 tip

87
00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:50.723
at your restaurant.
(audience claps)

88
00:04:58.462 --> 00:05:00.210
Thank you so much.

89
00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:01.340
Well, it's so fitting, 'cause Field Roast

90
00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.600
is a plant-based meat and cheese company

91
00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.040
who's committed to bringing bold flavor to your plates

92
00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.630
at home and restaurants across the country.

93
00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:13.270
And Diana, how you're able to raise these funds

94
00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:14.310
and the way you're giving them,

95
00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:17.100
you're such an inspiration, and you really blew our minds.

96
00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:20.549
So thank you for allowing us in on the party.

97
00:05:20.549 --> 00:05:25.549
And thank you to Field Roast and Diana

98
00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.410
and Julia and the gentlemen.

99
00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.620
Don't mess with Julia.

100
00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.400
And for more information,

101
00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:34.330 line:15%
on how you can support Diana's initiative.

102
00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:36.350 line:15%
I say this with like fingers pointing,

103
00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.070 line:15%
'cause I'm so passionate about it.

104
00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.140 line:15%
Visit our website please.

105
00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:44.110 line:15%
And we would love to eat at your restaurant

106
00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.520
as soon as it's safe and possible.

107
00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:51.520
We celebrate you Julia, and Diana and gentlemen, thank you.

108
00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:54.848
Thank you so much for being on the show today.

109
00:05:54.848 --> 00:05:58.007
(audience claps)

110
00:05:58.007 --> 00:06:00.674 line:15%
(upbeat music)

